# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The home page used to live at home.html, with index.html a stub that carried
# no content and bounced to it with a meta refresh plus location.replace. A
# browser followed that fine. A crawler landing on the apex did not: it got
# 1.3 KB of "Redirecting..." with nothing to read, and anything that would not
# run the script saw no site at all. Google's AdSense ad-placement preview was
# the case that surfaced it - it reported "We can't find the page you're
# looking for" for getpolytechniques.com while the site was plainly up.
#
# The home page is now index.html, so the apex serves the real thing with a
# 200 and no hop. These two rules keep every existing link and bookmark to the
# old address working, as a real server-side redirect rather than a scripted
# one. 301 rather than 302 because the move is permanent and the ranking
# signal should follow.
/home       /   301
/home.html  /   301
